## Day 3 takeaways:
"Learning" = error minimization. Training is a loop: predict → measure error (loss) → adjust weights downhill (gradient descent) → repeat. Nothing mystical.
Azure ML = DevOps for models. Workspace holds everything; compute clusters scale to zero; every training run is logged like a CI build.
Three build paths: AutoML (no data scientists → exam answer), Designer (drag-and-drop), notebooks (code-first).
Deployment tell: per-transaction/instant → real-time endpoint; millions of rows on a schedule → batch endpoint.
The lifecycle is a loop, not a line. Models decay — data drift is the ML equivalent of a slow memory leak, and monitoring deployed models is a APM skillset applied to AI.
